<%
  /*
   * The IndusNetwork mark, beneath the sign-in card.
   *
   * This was a built plate: the IndusDefender owl and a light chip holding the
   * network lock-up, side by side under a "Powered & Secured By" label, with
   * the wordmark and "Protect. Prevent. Prevail." set in text so they could
   * take this directory's palette. It is now the single supplied banner
   * instead — one image, no typed matter, and no IndusDefender.
   *
   * The artwork carries its own navy-to-maroon ground, so it needs no plate
   * under it: the vellum panel and rule the old badge borrowed from the rest
   * of the application would only draw a second box around a picture that is
   * already a box. What it keeps is the corner radius, which is the one thing
   * that would otherwise mark it as foreign on a page where every other edge
   * is rounded.
   *
   * The file is 520x235 and sits flush — the logo is centred inside its own
   * generous margin, so cropping or padding it would only double that space.
   */
%>
<div class="indus-badge">
  <img class="indus-banner" src="<%= base %>/images/indus-network-banner.jpg"
       alt="INDUSNETWORK.ORG — Collaboration Creates Success."
       width="520" height="235" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
</div>
